cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this corpus, cite the project as below."
title: "Libertas Andrews–Curtis Conjecture"
abstract: >-
  A machine-checked Lean 4 corpus for the Andrews–Curtis conjecture: 81 modules,
  1,553 declarations and eight registered theorems, including a kernel-checked
  reduction of the conjecture to a single open input. Produced in three days by
  the Libertas Superintelligence platform and its proprietary Cognitive World
  Models, which construct explicit world models for the specific problem or
  domain being addressed; in this run the world model attempted to build a map
  of the path to a solution and recorded each reasoning step from requirement to
  compiled theorem. The corpus is one stress test of the platform; Libertas
  Technology Group focuses on applied and industrial applications.
